{#
  Router prompt. Output is constrained to RouteDecision's JSON schema by the
  backend, so this prompt only has to make the categories separable.

  Each category is defined by the shape of the question, not its topic: the
  3B model read topical definitions ("errors, exceptions, validation") as a
  reason to call nearly everything a bug — 31% on the dev set. Shape cues and
  two examples per route took it to 87.5%, and to 88.9% (16/18) on the
  bug/architecture/dependency/locator dev set. Both remaining dev misses are
  questions a human could file either way.

  Tuned on evaluation/datasets/router_dev.jsonl, disjoint from
  tests/fixtures/router_questions.jsonl, and the examples are not about
  petclinic, so the held-out score is not fitted to the questions it is
  measured on. Re-tune on the dev set, never on the held-out questions.
#}
Classify a question about a software repository into exactly one category.

- bug: asks WHY something fails, errors, throws, or behaves wrongly. Usually starts with "Why does/would ... fail".
- architecture: asks HOW something is designed, configured, defined or structured. Usually starts with "How is/are/does".
- dependency: asks WHICH classes or components use, call, inherit from, or interact with something. Usually starts with "Which" or "What classes/components".
- locator: asks WHERE something is — which file or class contains it. Usually starts with "Where is".

Examples:
Q: Why does POST /orders sometimes return 500?
{"route": "bug"}
Q: Why would the login form reject a valid password?
{"route": "bug"}
Q: How is request authentication wired into the web layer?
{"route": "architecture"}
Q: How are database migrations configured at startup?
{"route": "architecture"}
Q: Which services call the PaymentGateway client?
{"route": "dependency"}
Q: What components are involved when an invoice is emailed?
{"route": "dependency"}
Q: Where is the class that parses uploaded CSV files?
{"route": "locator"}
Q: Where is the endpoint that deletes a user account?
{"route": "locator"}

Q: {{ question }}
